Thanks for the detailed bug report.

Fix here: https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/55351

This will be fixed in .NET 9 but I think you can work around it in .NET 8 with some middleware.

Add this to the start of the middleware pipeline before `UseForwardedHeaders()`:

```cs
app.Use(async (context, next) =>
{
    var scheme = context.Request.Scheme;
    await next();
    context.Request.Scheme = scheme;
});
```

That should restore the original scheme before the request ends and the counter is decreased.
